@page "/templates"
@attribute [InteractiveServer]

<h1>Templates, generics and @@key</h1>

<p>Exercises <code>RenderFragment&lt;T&gt;</code>, a <code>@@typeparam</code> component and
<code>@@key</code>-driven diffing. All three depend on the generated component descriptor carrying an
open generic definition and a templated parameter, rather than on reflection over the closed type.</p>

<TypedList Id="names" Items="_names" Context="name">
    <ItemTemplate><strong>@name.ToUpperInvariant()</strong></ItemTemplate>
</TypedList>

<TypedList Id="numbers" Items="_numbers" Context="n">
    <ItemTemplate>#@(n * 2)</ItemTemplate>
</TypedList>

<button id="reverse" @onclick="Reverse">Reverse</button>

@code {
    private List<string> _names = ["alpha", "beta", "gamma"];
    private readonly List<int> _numbers = [1, 2, 3];

    // Reversing a @key-ed list moves the existing elements instead of re-rendering them in place,
    // which is what makes the key path observable from a test.
    private void Reverse() => _names = [.. Enumerable.Reverse(_names)];
}
